{"text": "thirteen", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">thirttene</i>, variant (through metathesis) of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">thrittene</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">\u00fer\u0113ot\u012bene</i>, from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*\u00feritehun</i>, compound of <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*\u00fer\u012bz</i> (\u201cthree\u201d) + <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*tehun</i> (\u201cteen\u201d). Cognate with West Frisian <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fy\">trettjin</i>, Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">dertien</i>, German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">dreizehn</i>, Danish <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"da\">tretten</i>. Equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">three</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-teen</i>.\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8\u03b8\u025c\u02d0.ti\u02d0n/"], ["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02cc\u03b8\u025c\u02d0\u02c8ti\u02d0n/"]]}